// ONE CUSTODY AUTHORITY FOR CREDENTIALS DELIVERED FROM SECRET MANAGER TO A FLEET HOST FILE.
//
// gunbc#11679 landed this module as the microVM controller's App-key converge, with root:root 0400
// and a root-only directory spelled as constants. The second credential with the same shape -- the
// ntfy publisher token the approval broker publishes with (gunbc.auth.approval_request_submission
// read_publisher_token) -- was a HumanIntervention: an operator created it and wrote it where the
// unit could read it. Rather than a sibling module per credential (a second custody home, DESIGN
// §3) or one fleet-converge mode per credential (a hand-enumerated mode roster that grows with
// every secret), the constants became the FIELDS OF A ROW and the credential became a DISPATCH
// CHOICE over a CLOSED ROSTER of rows. The controller key is the first row; its root:root 0400 is
// that row's data, not a special case beside the roster.
//
// WHAT A ROW CARRIES. The SecretRef, the path, the host scope, the file's owner and group
// principals and its MODE ARM, and the DIRECTORY's owner, group and mode arm. The directory is a
// row field because a group-readable token is unreadable by that group unless the group can
// TRAVERSE the directory: a 0640 root:gunbc-ntfy token needs a 0750 root:gunbc-ntfy directory, and
// the predecessor's check refused every group bit on the directory. That refusal was right for a
// root-only key and wrong for a service token, so it is now DERIVED from the row's directory arm
// rather than relaxed.
//
// MODE IS A CLOSED ARM, NEVER A CALLER OCTAL. Both far-side legs are derived from the arm: the
// exact-mode leg (`-perm 0400` / `-perm 0640`) and the forbidden-bits leg (`-perm /077` /
// `-perm /037`), and likewise for the directory (`0700` + `/077`, `0750` + `/027`). The owner leg
// takes `-user`/`-group` from the row.
//
// ROW ADMISSION REFUSES THE INCOHERENT PAIRING BEFORE ANY FETCH. A row whose file grants its group
// read under a directory that denies that group traversal would deliver a token its reader cannot
// open while the readback reported the file exactly as declared -- green on every leg and useless.
// custody_row_placement refuses it, typed and located (CustodyGroupCannotTraverse), rather than
// widening the directory to make it work (DESIGN §5 absorbing fallback).
//
// WHAT THE READBACK ESTABLISHES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. This caveat is load-bearing and must not be
// lost in a later edit. The find-metadata readback below establishes which principals HOLD
// PERMISSION BITS on the file and its directories. It does NOT establish that a principal without
// those bits cannot open the file -- an ACL, a capability, a bind mount or a second hard link are
// all outside what `find -perm -user -group` observes -- and establishing that needs a leg that
// EXECUTES AS ANOTHER USER and is refused. gunbc.rung_drop approval_store_single_writer_by_agreement
// names exactly that stronger observation as its restoration trigger and names a permission-bits
// readback among the things that do NOT retire it. So this module is NECESSARY-BUT-NOT-SUFFICIENT
// for that trigger; citing a HELD receipt from here as retiring it is §4b(1) rung inflation.
//
// THE CUSTODY THE CONTROLLER ROW NARROWS. The shared-slot path still reads gunbc.runner_unit_file
// runner_host_app_pem_path (/etc/actions-runner/app.pem), owned by the RUNNER USER. That file is
// deliberately NOT touched here: the shared-slot path is X in a replacement migration (DESIGN §3),
// still load-bearing. The controller row establishes the Y-side custody -- a copy whose permission
// bits admit root alone, outside every jail and attempt root. Nothing here selects the microVM path.
//
// THE FETCH IS TYPED, NOT A PRELUDE: gunbc.auth.secret_ref_credential fetch_secret_ref_credential
// over the run's workload-identity token, refusing a response about a different version than the
// one requested. The plaintext never touches the near-side disk.
//
// DIGEST, STATED AS WHAT IS ACTUALLY CHECKED. .dag has no SHA-256 over a String, so the comparison
// is converge_typed_remote_file's far-side `cmp -s -` against the fetched version's exact bytes on
// stdin -- byte equality, which is stronger than a digest match. The receipt names the resolved
// version identity, never the bytes.
//
// PLAINTEXT STAGING. The only staging is the far-side sibling <path>.gunbc-staging, inside the row's
// directory, verified BEFORE the stage leg runs. For a root-only row no non-root uid can traverse
// to it. For a group row the staging file is briefly root:root with the far side's umask before its
// chmod; the directory admits only root and the row's group, which is the principal the token is
// delivered TO, so the window exposes nothing beyond the declared reader. It is removed after every
// attempt WHOSE ANCESTOR AND DIRECTORY AUTHORITY HAS BEEN ESTABLISHED -- never beneath a path the
// route declined to trust, because `rm` is a root mutation through that same path (see
// StagingCleanupAuthorization, carried over from gunbc#11902). Its absence is READ BACK from a
// listing of its parent; a failed removal, a surviving sibling, or a withheld cleanup refuses the
// run (the cleanup-is-part-of-the-mint rule of gunbc.secret_provision_actuator).

// ── The closed roster (pure) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// A CLOSED COPRODUCT, NOT A STRING. The dispatch input is a choice whose options are this roster's
// wire names, and the entry maps the chosen word back through the roster, so an unrostered word is
// a typed refusal and there is no free-text path to a SecretRef.
type HostCustodyCredential
  = ControllerAppKey
  | ApprovalNtfyPublisherToken
  | FabricStateWriterKey
  | CursorWorkerTurnApiKey
  | CodexWorkerTurnAuth
  | OracleOciApiSigningKey
  | ClaudeCodeOauthHarnessToken

data host_custody_credential_roster: List<HostCustodyCredential> = [ControllerAppKey, ApprovalNtfyPublisherToken, FabricStateWriterKey, CursorWorkerTurnApiKey, CodexWorkerTurnAuth, OracleOciApiSigningKey, ClaudeCodeOauthHarnessToken]

fn host_custody_credential_wire(c: HostCustodyCredential) -> String {
  match c {
    ControllerAppKey => "controller_app_key"
    ApprovalNtfyPublisherToken => "approval_ntfy_publisher_token"
    FabricStateWriterKey => "fabric_state_writer_key"
    CursorWorkerTurnApiKey => "cursor_worker_turn_api_key"
    CodexWorkerTurnAuth => "codex_worker_turn_auth"
    OracleOciApiSigningKey => "oracle_oci_api_signing_key"
    ClaudeCodeOauthHarnessToken => "claude_code_oauth_harness_token"
  }
}

// WHO HOLDS THE CURRENT VALUE AFTER PLACEMENT. Every row but one is store-authoritative: the secret
// is the truth and the host copy is converged to it. The codex subscription auth.json is not: codex
// rotates its refresh token on the host while it runs (extdeps.llm.codex_auth
// codex_source_refresh_persistence), so after placement the HOST holds the live token and the store
// lags until this converge reads the host file back and adds it as a new version. Overwriting that
// host file from the store would put a spent token back, and so would placing the store's copy on a
// second host. That is why a host-authoritative row must name exactly one host (placement refuses
// otherwise) and why its converge never writes over a file that is already there.
type CustodyAuthority
  = CustodyStoreAuthoritative
  | CustodyHostAuthoritativeAfterPlacement

fn host_custody_authority(c: HostCustodyCredential) -> CustodyAuthority {
  match c {
    ControllerAppKey => CustodyStoreAuthoritative
    ApprovalNtfyPublisherToken => CustodyStoreAuthoritative
    FabricStateWriterKey => CustodyStoreAuthoritative
    CursorWorkerTurnApiKey => CustodyStoreAuthoritative
    CodexWorkerTurnAuth => CustodyHostAuthoritativeAfterPlacement
    OracleOciApiSigningKey => CustodyStoreAuthoritative
    ClaudeCodeOauthHarnessToken => CustodyStoreAuthoritative
  }
}

data host_custody_credential_options: List<String> = map(host_custody_credential_roster, c => host_custody_credential_wire(c: c))

type HostCustodyCredentialSelection
  = HostCustodyCredentialSelected { credential: HostCustodyCredential }
  | HostCustodyCredentialUnrostered { supplied: String }

fn select_host_custody_credential(supplied: String) -> HostCustodyCredentialSelection {
  let word = trim(s: supplied)
  fold(host_custody_credential_roster, init: HostCustodyCredentialUnrostered { supplied: word }, f: (acc, c) =>
    match acc {
      HostCustodyCredentialSelected { credential: _ } => acc
      HostCustodyCredentialUnrostered { supplied: _ } =>
        if host_custody_credential_wire(c: c) == word { HostCustodyCredentialSelected { credential: c } } else { acc }
    }
  )
}

// THE FILE'S MODE ARM. Each arm derives the write mode, the exact-mode leg, the forbidden-bits leg,
// and whether it grants the group read -- four facts, one match each, no octal parameter anywhere.
type CustodyFileMode
  = CustodyFileOwnerRead
  | CustodyFileOwnerReadWrite
  | CustodyFileOwnerReadWriteGroupRead

fn custody_file_remote_mode(m: CustodyFileMode) -> RemoteFileMode {
  match m {
    CustodyFileOwnerRead => RemoteFileModeOwnerRead
    CustodyFileOwnerReadWrite => RemoteFileModeOwnerReadWrite
    CustodyFileOwnerReadWriteGroupRead => RemoteFileModeOwnerReadWriteGroupRead
  }
}

// THE EXACT-MODE LEG IS DERIVED FROM THE WRITE MODE, NOT RE-SPELLED BESIDE IT (review 69522). This
// used to match the arm and return its own octal literal, which made the mode a file is WRITTEN at
// and the mode it is ASSERTED at two independent facts that could drift apart -- and the drift would
// have been silent in the source and visible only as a readback refusal on a live host. The write
// mode's octal is owned by gunbc.typed_remote_file_write remote_file_mode_octal, so the readback leg
// asks that authority and prefixes the leading zero find(1) wants. One home, one octal (DESIGN §3).
fn custody_file_exact_perm(m: CustodyFileMode) -> String {
  join(["0", remote_file_mode_octal(mode: custody_file_remote_mode(m: m))], "")
}

fn custody_file_forbidden_perm(m: CustodyFileMode) -> String {
  match m {
    CustodyFileOwnerRead => "/077"
    CustodyFileOwnerReadWrite => "/077"
    CustodyFileOwnerReadWriteGroupRead => "/037"
  }
}

fn custody_file_grants_group(m: CustodyFileMode) -> Bool {
  match m {
    CustodyFileOwnerRead => false
    CustodyFileOwnerReadWrite => false
    CustodyFileOwnerReadWriteGroupRead => true
  }
}

// THE DIRECTORY'S MODE ARM, the field the predecessor did not have -- IMPORTED, not declared here.
// It was a local CustodyDirMode whose two arms returned the octal literals "0700" and "0750", and
// the second of those is the mode gunbc.auth.approval_ntfy_converge also declared for the ntfy
// config directory, which the ntfy row below ensures too. One directory, two authorities for its
// mode, reconciled by a witness holding the two strings equal -- validation standing where
// construction was available (§5). The arm now lives in gunbc.managed_directory, which is the
// module that already owns what mode a fleet-owned host directory gets and already renders octals
// through extdeps.access.posix rather than spelling them.
//
// THE FORBIDDEN MASK STAYS HERE because it is not a mode. It is the complement find(1) needs for
// the readback leg (`-perm /027`), a fact about how THIS converge proves a directory is not looser
// than it should be, and no other consumer of the arm asks it.
fn custody_dir_exact_perm(m: DeclaredDirectoryMode) -> String {
  declared_directory_mode_octal(m: m)
}

fn custody_dir_forbidden_perm(m: DeclaredDirectoryMode) -> String {
  match m {
    DirectoryOwnerOnly => "/077"
    DirectoryOwnerAllGroupTraverse => "/027"
    DirectoryOwnerAllEveryoneTraverse => "/022"
  }
}

fn custody_dir_grants_group_traverse(m: DeclaredDirectoryMode) -> Bool {
  declared_directory_grants_group_traverse(m: m)
}

// Principals by NAME (extdeps.posix.identity PosixOwnerNames), because find(1)'s -user/-group and
// chown(1) both take names and a service account's numeric ids are allocated per host
// (gunbc.fleet_posix_accounts), not declared.
type CustodyHostScope
  = CustodyAnyRunnerHost
  | CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: HostIdentity }

type HostCredentialCustodyRow {
  credential: HostCustodyCredential
  secret: SecretRef
  path: NonEmptyStr
  host_scope: CustodyHostScope
  file_ownership: PosixOwnerNames
  file_mode: CustodyFileMode
  dir_ownership: PosixOwnerNames
  dir_mode: DeclaredDirectoryMode
}

// The controller key's path is the signer's own key reference (gunbc.github_effect_perform
// lifecycle_controller_app_key), never re-spelled; HostKeyFile is the only arm that names a file.
fn signing_key_file_path(key: JwsSigningKeyRef) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match key {
    HostKeyFile { path: p } => p
  }
}

data custody_root_only: PosixOwnerNames = PosixOwnerNames {
  user: fleet_posix_root_user.name,
  group: fleet_posix_root_user.name,
}

// THE DIRECTORY IS NOT THIS CONVERGE'S TO DESCRIBE, so neither leg is restated here. It is the ntfy
// server's config directory, which gunbc.auth.approval_ntfy_converge NtfyConfigDirectory also
// ensures; two converges asserting different ownership or modes on one directory would flap it on
// every run. The group comes from approval_ntfy_principal_name and the mode from
// approval_ntfy_dir_mode, both declared by the deployment that owns the directory, so agreement is
// by construction rather than by a witness holding two values equal.
data custody_root_owned_ntfy_group: PosixOwnerNames = PosixOwnerNames {
  user: fleet_posix_root_user.name,
  group: approval_ntfy_principal_name,
}

// THE FABRIC STATE KEY'S READER GROUP. The key was root:<operator> 0640, so reading it meant being
// the operator's group, and the deploy principal (the CI job user, ghrunner) got there by a hand
// `usermod -aG <operator> ghrunner` that made it a member of the service user's whole group. The key
// is now owned by a group that exists for it alone; custody_reader_set declares who is in it and the
// converge reads that membership back.
data fabric_state_key_reader_group: NonEmptyStr = "gunbc-fabric-state-key"

data custody_root_owned_fabric_state_key_group: PosixOwnerNames = PosixOwnerNames {
  user: fleet_posix_root_user.name,
  group: fabric_state_key_reader_group,
}

data custody_operator_only: PosixOwnerNames = PosixOwnerNames {
  user: fleet_posix_operator_user.name,
  group: fleet_posix_operator_user.name,
}

// THE WORKER-TURN CREDENTIALS live on srv2, the host the declared Cursor offer and the codex harness
// turns dispatch on, owned by the operator account the dispatch spawns run as. Cursor's key is
// read-only on the host. The codex directory IS the turn's CODEX_HOME: codex writes auth.json,
// sessions and logs beneath it, so the directory and the file are owner read-write.

// OracleOciApiSigningKey signs every OCI request gunbc.oracle_oci.compartment_ensure makes, through
// the signer's own key reference, never re-spelled. It is delivered to srv1 only, root-owned and
// owner-read, because srv1 is where the OCI converge runs and nothing else signs with it.
fn host_credential_custody_row(c: HostCustodyCredential) -> HostCredentialCustodyRow {
  match c {
    FabricStateWriterKey => HostCredentialCustodyRow {
      credential: c, secret: fabric_state_key_secret_ref, path: fabric_state_key_host_path,
      host_scope: CustodyAnyRunnerHost,
      file_ownership: custody_root_owned_fabric_state_key_group,
      file_mode: CustodyFileOwnerReadWriteGroupRead,
      dir_ownership: custody_root_owned_fabric_state_key_group,
      dir_mode: DirectoryOwnerAllGroupTraverse,
    }

    ControllerAppKey => HostCredentialCustodyRow {
      credential: c,
      secret: gunbai_ci_app_pem_secret,
      path: signing_key_file_path(key: lifecycle_controller_app_key),
      host_scope: CustodyAnyRunnerHost,
      file_ownership: custody_root_only,
      file_mode: CustodyFileOwnerRead,
      dir_ownership: custody_root_only,
      dir_mode: DirectoryOwnerOnly,
    }
    CursorWorkerTurnApiKey => HostCredentialCustodyRow {
      credential: c,
      secret: cursor_api_key_harness_secret_ref,
      path: cursor_worker_turn_api_key_host_path,
      host_scope: CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: cursor_worker_turn_custody_host },
      file_ownership: custody_operator_only,
      file_mode: CustodyFileOwnerRead,
      dir_ownership: custody_operator_only,
      dir_mode: DirectoryOwnerOnly,
    }
    CodexWorkerTurnAuth => HostCredentialCustodyRow {
      credential: c,
      secret: codex_auth_harness_secret_ref,
      path: codex_worker_turn_auth_host_path,
      host_scope: CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: codex_worker_turn_custody_host },
      file_ownership: custody_operator_only,
      file_mode: CustodyFileOwnerReadWrite,
      dir_ownership: custody_operator_only,
      dir_mode: DirectoryOwnerOnly,
    }
    OracleOciApiSigningKey => HostCredentialCustodyRow {
      credential: c,
      secret: oci_api_signing_key_secret_ref,
      path: signing_key_file_path(key: oci_api_signing_key),
      host_scope: CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: operator_host_srv1 },
      file_ownership: custody_root_only,
      file_mode: CustodyFileOwnerRead,
      dir_ownership: custody_root_only,
      dir_mode: DirectoryOwnerOnly,
    }
    ClaudeCodeOauthHarnessToken => HostCredentialCustodyRow {
      credential: c,
      secret: claude_code_oauth_harness_secret_ref,
      path: claude_code_oauth_harness_host_path,
      host_scope: CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: operator_host_srv1 },
      file_ownership: PosixOwnerNames { user: fleet_posix_root_user.name, group: fleet_posix_operator_user.name },
      file_mode: CustodyFileOwnerReadWriteGroupRead,
      dir_ownership: PosixOwnerNames { user: fleet_posix_root_user.name, group: fleet_posix_operator_user.name },
      dir_mode: DirectoryOwnerAllGroupTraverse,
    }
    ApprovalNtfyPublisherToken => HostCredentialCustodyRow {
      credential: c,
      secret: approval_ntfy_publisher_token_secret_ref,
      path: approval_publisher_token_path,
      host_scope: CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: operator_host_srv1 },
      file_ownership: custody_root_owned_ntfy_group,
      file_mode: CustodyFileOwnerReadWriteGroupRead,
      dir_ownership: custody_root_owned_ntfy_group,
      dir_mode: approval_ntfy_dir_mode,
    }
  }
}

// ── The reader set (pure) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// WHO MAY READ A GROUP-READABLE CREDENTIAL IS A DECLARED SET, NOT A CONSEQUENCE OF WHICH GROUP THE
// FILE HAPPENS TO CARRY. Present only where a row's group exists for the credential alone; every
// other row's group is an account's own primary group, whose membership this converge does not own.
// The deploy principal is the host's job user (RunnerHostSpec.job_user), never a literal, because the
// job user is per host (gunbc.fleet_posix_accounts srv1_ci_deploy_runner_principal). The other member is
// the service that serves the key: the dashboard runs as the operator account on srv1.
type CustodyReaderSet {
  group: NonEmptyStr
  members: List<NonEmptyStr>
}

fn custody_reader_set(c: HostCustodyCredential, job_user: NonEmptyStr) -> CustodyReaderSet? {
  match c {
    FabricStateWriterKey =>
      Present { value: CustodyReaderSet { group: fabric_state_key_reader_group, members: [fleet_posix_operator_user.name, job_user] } }
    ControllerAppKey => none
    ApprovalNtfyPublisherToken => none
    CursorWorkerTurnApiKey => none
    CodexWorkerTurnAuth => none
    OracleOciApiSigningKey => none
    ClaudeCodeOauthHarnessToken => none
  }
}

// WHAT A getent READBACK CAN SAY, EACH ARM A DIFFERENT REMEDY. An unexpected member is a WIDEN and
// refuses before any mutation; a missing member is a grant that has not landed; an absent group is a
// first run; unobservable is a broken probe and is never read as either.
type CustodyReadersStanding
  = CustodyReadersNotDeclared
  | CustodyReadersAsDeclared { group: NonEmptyStr }
  | CustodyReadersUnexpectedMember { group: NonEmptyStr, unexpected: List<String> }
  | CustodyReadersMissingMember { group: NonEmptyStr, missing: List<String> }
  | CustodyReadersGroupAbsent { group: NonEmptyStr }
  | CustodyReadersUnobservable { group: NonEmptyStr, reason: String }

// `getent group NAME` prints name:password:gid:member,member and exits 2 when the key is absent.
fn custody_getent_group_argv(group: NonEmptyStr) -> List<String> {
  ["getent", "group", group as String]
}

// groupadd -f exits 0 when the group already exists (groupadd(8)), so creation is idempotent by the
// tool's own contract and needs no existence pre-check.
fn custody_groupadd_argv(group: NonEmptyStr) -> List<String> {
  ["groupadd", "-f", "--", group as String]
}

// gpasswd -a APPENDS one login. The converge never replaces the member list (-M), so it cannot
// silently remove a member it did not read first.
fn custody_group_add_member_argv(group: NonEmptyStr, login: String) -> List<String> {
  ["gpasswd", "-a", login, group as String]
}

fn custody_group_member_names(stdout: String) -> List<String> {
  let fields = split(s: trim(s: stdout), delimiter: ":")
  if length(fields) != 4 { [] } else { filter(xs: map(split(s: last_or_empty(xs: fields), delimiter: ","), m => trim(s: m)), f: m => m != "") }
}

fn classify_custody_readers(declared: CustodyReaderSet?, exit_code: Int, stdout: String, stderr: String) -> CustodyReadersStanding {
  match declared {
    Absent => CustodyReadersNotDeclared
    Present { value: d } =>
      if exit_code == 2 {
        CustodyReadersGroupAbsent { group: d.group }
      } else if exit_code != 0 {
        CustodyReadersUnobservable { group: d.group, reason: join(["getent exit=", to_string(exit_code), " ", trim(s: stderr)], "") }
      } else if length(split(s: trim(s: stdout), delimiter: ":")) != 4 {
        CustodyReadersUnobservable { group: d.group, reason: concat("getent printed no group record: ", trim(s: stdout)) }
      } else {
        let observed = custody_group_member_names(stdout: stdout)
        let want = map(d.members, m => m as String)
        let unexpected = filter(xs: observed, f: m => !any(want, w => w == m))
        let missing = filter(xs: want, f: w => !any(observed, m => m == w))
        if length(unexpected) > 0 {
          CustodyReadersUnexpectedMember { group: d.group, unexpected: unexpected }
        } else if length(missing) > 0 {
          CustodyReadersMissingMember { group: d.group, missing: missing }
        } else {
          CustodyReadersAsDeclared { group: d.group }
        }
      }
  }
}

fn custody_readers_wire(s: CustodyReadersStanding) -> String {
  match s {
    CustodyReadersNotDeclared => "not-declared"
    CustodyReadersAsDeclared { group: g } => concat("AS-DECLARED group=", g as String)
    CustodyReadersUnexpectedMember { group: g, unexpected: u } => join(["UNEXPECTED-MEMBER group=", g as String, " members=", join(u, ",")], "")
    CustodyReadersMissingMember { group: g, missing: m } => join(["MISSING-MEMBER group=", g as String, " members=", join(m, ",")], "")
    CustodyReadersGroupAbsent { group: g } => concat("GROUP-ABSENT group=", g as String)
    CustodyReadersUnobservable { group: g, reason: r } => join(["UNOBSERVABLE group=", g as String, " ", r], "")
  }
}

// Mutation is decided from the BEFORE reading alone. Unexpected and unobservable refuse with no
// write: widening the set by appending beside a member nobody declared is the silent widen.
type CustodyReadersAction
  = CustodyReadersNothingToDo
  | CustodyReadersCreateAndAdd { group: NonEmptyStr, add: List<String> }
  | CustodyReadersAdd { group: NonEmptyStr, add: List<String> }
  | CustodyReadersRefused { reason: String }

fn custody_readers_action(declared: CustodyReaderSet?, before: CustodyReadersStanding) -> CustodyReadersAction {
  match before {
    CustodyReadersNotDeclared => CustodyReadersNothingToDo
    CustodyReadersAsDeclared { group: _ } => CustodyReadersNothingToDo
    CustodyReadersUnexpectedMember { group: _, unexpected: _ } => CustodyReadersRefused { reason: concat("reader group has an undeclared member: ", custody_readers_wire(s: before)) }
    CustodyReadersUnobservable { group: _, reason: _ } => CustodyReadersRefused { reason: concat("reader group unobservable: ", custody_readers_wire(s: before)) }
    CustodyReadersMissingMember { group: g, missing: m } => CustodyReadersAdd { group: g, add: m }
    CustodyReadersGroupAbsent { group: g } =>
      match declared {
        Present { value: d } => CustodyReadersCreateAndAdd { group: g, add: map(d.members, x => x as String) }
        Absent => CustodyReadersNothingToDo
      }
  }
}

// ── Row admission (pure) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

data custody_forbidden_tree: FileTreeScope = FileTreeScope { root_path: fabric_cell_base_dir as NonEmptyStr }

type CustodyPlacementRefusal
  = CustodyPathInForbiddenTree { path: NonEmptyStr }
  | CustodyPathOutsideScope { path: NonEmptyStr }
  | CustodyPathNoDedicatedDirectory { path: NonEmptyStr }
  | CustodyGroupCannotTraverse { path: NonEmptyStr, dir: NonEmptyStr, group: NonEmptyStr, file_perm: String, dir_perm: String }
  | CustodyDirectoryGroupDiffers { path: NonEmptyStr, file_group: NonEmptyStr, dir_group: NonEmptyStr }
  | CustodyHostAuthoritativeNotSingleHost { path: NonEmptyStr }

type CustodyPlacement
  = CustodyPlaced { row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, key_dir: NonEmptyStr, upper_ancestors: List<String> }
  | CustodyPlacementRefused { cause: CustodyPlacementRefusal }

fn custody_placement_refusal_wire(r: CustodyPlacementRefusal) -> String {
  match r {
    CustodyPathInForbiddenTree { path: p } =>
      join(["custody path ", p as String, " is inside the fabric-cell tree ", fabric_cell_base_dir, ", which roots every attempt and jail"], "")
    CustodyPathOutsideScope { path: p } =>
      join(["custody path ", p as String, " is outside ", runner_host_file_scope.root_path as String], "")
    CustodyPathNoDedicatedDirectory { path: p } =>
      join(["custody path ", p as String, " has no dedicated directory below ", runner_host_file_scope.root_path as String, " whose mode the row can own"], "")
    CustodyGroupCannotTraverse { path: p, dir: d, group: g, file_perm: fp, dir_perm: dp } =>
      join(["custody row for ", p as String, " grants group ", g as String, " read (", fp, ") but its directory ", d as String, " is declared ", dp, ", which denies that group traversal -- the reader could not open the file the readback would report as held"], "")
    CustodyDirectoryGroupDiffers { path: p, file_group: fg, dir_group: dg } =>
      join(["custody row for ", p as String, " grants group ", fg as String, " read but its directory is group ", dg as String, ", so the file's group has no traversal through it"], "")
    CustodyHostAuthoritativeNotSingleHost { path: p } =>
      join(["custody row for ", p as String, " is host-authoritative after placement and must name exactly one host; a second host would receive the store's lagging, possibly spent, copy"], "")
  }
}

fn last_or_empty(xs: List<String>) -> String {
  fold(xs, init: "", f: fn(_, x) { x })
}

// The directory and its ancestors derive from the row's one path, never re-spelled. The group
// clauses are the row-model repair: a group-readable file requires a group-traversable directory
// owned by THAT group, and neither half is widened to make the pairing work.
fn custody_row_placement(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow) -> CustodyPlacement {
  let key_path = row.path
  let ancestors = runner_host_path_ancestors(path: key_path as String)
  let dir = last_or_empty(xs: ancestors)
  let host_authoritative_on_many = match host_custody_authority(c: row.credential) {
    CustodyStoreAuthoritative => false
    CustodyHostAuthoritativeAfterPlacement =>
      match row.host_scope {
        CustodyAnyRunnerHost => true
        CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: _ } => false
      }
  }
  if host_authoritative_on_many {
    CustodyPlacementRefused { cause: CustodyHostAuthoritativeNotSingleHost { path: key_path } }
  } else if path_within_file_tree_scope(scope: custody_forbidden_tree, path: key_path) {
    CustodyPlacementRefused { cause: CustodyPathInForbiddenTree { path: key_path } }
  } else if !path_within_file_tree_scope(scope: runner_host_file_scope, path: key_path) {
    CustodyPlacementRefused { cause: CustodyPathOutsideScope { path: key_path } }
  } else if dir == "" || dir == (runner_host_file_scope.root_path as String) {
    CustodyPlacementRefused { cause: CustodyPathNoDedicatedDirectory { path: key_path } }
  } else if custody_file_grants_group(m: row.file_mode) && !custody_dir_grants_group_traverse(m: row.dir_mode) {
    CustodyPlacementRefused {
      cause: CustodyGroupCannotTraverse {
        path: key_path,
        dir: dir as NonEmptyStr,
        group: row.file_ownership.group,
        file_perm: custody_file_exact_perm(m: row.file_mode),
        dir_perm: custody_dir_exact_perm(m: row.dir_mode),
      },
    }
  } else if custody_file_grants_group(m: row.file_mode) && (row.file_ownership.group as String) != (row.dir_ownership.group as String) {
    CustodyPlacementRefused {
      cause: CustodyDirectoryGroupDiffers { path: key_path, file_group: row.file_ownership.group, dir_group: row.dir_ownership.group },
    }
  } else {
    CustodyPlaced {
      row: row,
      key_dir: dir as NonEmptyStr,
      upper_ancestors: filter(ancestors, a => a != dir),
    }
  }
}

// ── Readback vocabulary (pure) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// THE THREE FAR-SIDE QUESTIONS ONE PATH IS ASKED, each derived from the row. One find per clause so
// a refusal says WHICH clause failed; `%` cannot cross the SSH edge
// (gunbc.fleet_known_hosts_anchor portable_remote_word_char_allowed), so a stat format cannot.
type CustodyPathLegs {
  kind: String
  ownership: PosixOwnerNames
  exact_perm: String
  forbidden_perm: String
}

fn custody_file_legs(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow) -> CustodyPathLegs {
  CustodyPathLegs {
    kind: "f",
    ownership: row.file_ownership,
    exact_perm: custody_file_exact_perm(m: row.file_mode),
    forbidden_perm: custody_file_forbidden_perm(m: row.file_mode),
  }
}

fn custody_dir_legs(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow) -> CustodyPathLegs {
  CustodyPathLegs {
    kind: "d",
    ownership: row.dir_ownership,
    exact_perm: custody_dir_exact_perm(m: row.dir_mode),
    forbidden_perm: custody_dir_forbidden_perm(m: row.dir_mode),
  }
}

fn custody_owner_clause(o: PosixOwnerNames) -> List<String> {
  ["-user", o.user as String, "-group", o.group as String]
}

fn custody_perm_clause(perm: String) -> List<String> {
  ["-perm", perm]
}

type CustodyFindReading {
  owned_as_declared: Bool
  forbidden_bits: Bool
  exact_mode: Bool
}

type CustodyPathMetadata
  = CustodyPathAsDeclared
  | CustodyPathWrongOwner
  | CustodyPathForbiddenBits
  | CustodyPathModeNotDeclared
  | CustodyPathAbsent
  | CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: String }

// Owner first: a file owned by the wrong principal is the most dangerous state regardless of its
// mode, and reporting it as a mode defect would send the reader to chmod a file they do not own.
fn classify_custody_path(reading: CustodyFindReading) -> CustodyPathMetadata {
  if !reading.owned_as_declared {
    CustodyPathWrongOwner
  } else if reading.forbidden_bits {
    CustodyPathForbiddenBits
  } else if !reading.exact_mode {
    CustodyPathModeNotDeclared
  } else {
    CustodyPathAsDeclared
  }
}

fn custody_path_metadata_wire(m: CustodyPathMetadata, legs: CustodyPathLegs) -> String {
  let declared = join(["owner=", posix_owner_names_text(names: legs.ownership), " mode=", legs.exact_perm], "")
  match m {
    CustodyPathAsDeclared => declared
    CustodyPathWrongOwner => concat("WRONG-OWNER (declared ", concat(declared, ")"))
    CustodyPathForbiddenBits => join(["FORBIDDEN-BITS (mode has bits in ", legs.forbidden_perm, ")"], "")
    CustodyPathModeNotDeclared => concat("MODE-NOT-", legs.exact_perm)
    CustodyPathAbsent => "ABSENT"
    CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r } => concat("UNOBSERVABLE ", r)
  }
}

// THE STAGING SIBLING'S ABSENCE IS ESTABLISHED BY A SUCCESSFUL LISTING OF ITS PARENT, never by a
// failed read of the child (gunbc#11902): GNU `test -e` answers 1 for ENOENT, EACCES on an ancestor,
// ELOOP, ENOTDIR and EIO alike, so "gone" and "could not look" arrived as one value, and absence
// feeds CustodyHeld. The argv and the membership read are gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe's
// (parent_listing_argv, listing_contains_entry); only the TRANSPORT is this module's, because the
// parent admits root and at most the row's group, so an unelevated entry_presence could only ever
// answer Indeterminate -- a departure stated rather than silent (DESIGN §3b).
type StagingResidue
  = StagingAbsent
  | StagingResiduePresent { path: String }
  | StagingUnobservable { reason: String }

// CLEANUP IS A ROOT MUTATION, so it is entitled to the same path authority the WRITE is (gunbc#11902).
// The gate is PATH AUTHORITY and deliberately not the whole action: a content or file-metadata
// observation may be unobservable while the path is safely contained, and cleanup is still
// desirable there. So the seal joins three facts and nothing else -- upper ancestors PathsRootOnly,
// the directory exactly as the row declares it, and the staging path's parent being that admitted
// directory. sole_constructor makes an unauthorized cleanup UNWRITABLE: clear_staging DERIVES
// subject, parent, path and the residue predicate's key from the seal.
type StagingCleanupAuthorization sole_constructor {
  subject: CustodyHost
  parent: String
  staging: String
}

type StagingCleanupAdmission
  = StagingCleanupAuthorized { authorization: StagingCleanupAuthorization }
  | StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: String }

// THE ONLY MINT. PURE, over readings the caller already has: no leg runs here.
fn admit_staging_cleanup(
  subject: CustodyHost,
  upper_ancestors: RunnerHostPathMetadata,
  dir: CustodyPathMetadata,
  key_dir: String,
  staging: String,
) -> StagingCleanupAdmission {
  match upper_ancestors {
    PathsRootOnly =>
      match dir {
        CustodyPathAsDeclared =>
          if path_parent(path: staging) != key_dir {
            StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: join(["staging parent ", path_parent(path: staging), " is not the admitted directory ", key_dir], "") }
          } else {
            StagingCleanupAuthorized {
              authorization: StagingCleanupAuthorization { subject: subject, parent: key_dir, staging: staging },
            }
          }
        CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r } => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("directory metadata unobservable: ", r) }
        CustodyPathWrongOwner => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("directory is not as the row declares it: ", key_dir) }
        CustodyPathForbiddenBits => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("directory is not as the row declares it: ", key_dir) }
        CustodyPathModeNotDeclared => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("directory is not as the row declares it: ", key_dir) }
        CustodyPathAbsent => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("directory is not as the row declares it: ", key_dir) }
      }
    PathsNotRootOnly { paths: _, detail: _ } => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("an ancestor directory is not root-only: ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: upper_ancestors)) }
    PathsUnobservable { reason: _ } => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("an ancestor directory is not root-only: ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: upper_ancestors)) }
    PathsNotApplicable => StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: concat("an ancestor directory is not root-only: ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: upper_ancestors)) }
  }
}

// THE PREFIX, not the whole reason: the withheld arm carries WHICH joined fact failed through.
data staging_cleanup_withheld_reason: String = "staging cleanup withheld because path authority was not established"

// THE RESIDUE PREDICATE'S KEY IS DERIVED FROM THE SEAL, never supplied beside it. Carried from
// gunbc.microvm_controller_app_key_converge, which this module replaces, and hoisted to module-item
// grain there by #11941 just before the replacement deleted it -- the rationale outlives the module
// because the construction it explains does. As a free parameter, `name` was the one value of the
// three a caller could still spell freely, and it is exactly what this function keys on: a name that
// does not match the staging path's basename reads a listing CONTAINING the residue as
// StagingAbsent, and that false absence feeds a HELD verdict. The sole caller derives it as
// path_basename of the staging path for that reason (DESIGN §4b meta-obligation 1; §5, construction
// over validation).
//
// PURE, over a listing that SUCCEEDED; there is no exit code here to misread.
fn classify_staging_residue(path: String, name: String, stdout: String) -> StagingResidue {
  if listing_contains_entry(stdout: stdout, name: name) {
    StagingResiduePresent { path: path }
  } else {
    StagingAbsent
  }
}

fn staging_residue_wire(s: StagingResidue) -> String {
  match s {
    StagingAbsent => "absent"
    StagingResiduePresent { path: p } => concat("RESIDUE ", p)
    StagingUnobservable { reason: r } => concat("UNOBSERVABLE ", r)
  }
}

fn content_standing_wire(s: RunnerHostFileStanding) -> String {
  match s {
    HostFileIdentical => "identical-to-sm-version"
    HostFileDiffers => "DIFFERS-FROM-SM-VERSION"
    HostFileAbsent => "ABSENT"
    HostFileUnobservable { reason: r } => concat("UNOBSERVABLE ", r)
  }
}

// THE READBACK AND ITS VERDICT. Held requires every component, observed after the last mutation,
// and means only what the caveat at the top says: the declared principals hold exactly the declared
// permission bits. It is not an observation that anyone else was refused.
type CustodyReadback {
  file: CustodyPathMetadata
  dir: CustodyPathMetadata
  upper_ancestors: RunnerHostPathMetadata
  content: RunnerHostFileStanding
  staging: StagingResidue
  readers: CustodyReadersStanding
}

type CustodyStanding
  = CustodyHeld
  | CustodyNotHeld { causes: List<String> }

fn host_credential_custody(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, readback: CustodyReadback) -> CustodyStanding {
  let causes = concat(concat(concat(concat(concat(
    match readback.file {
      CustodyPathAsDeclared => []
      CustodyPathWrongOwner => [concat("file ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.file, legs: custody_file_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathForbiddenBits => [concat("file ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.file, legs: custody_file_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathModeNotDeclared => [concat("file ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.file, legs: custody_file_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathAbsent => [concat("file ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.file, legs: custody_file_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: _ } => [concat("file ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.file, legs: custody_file_legs(row: row)))]
    },
    match readback.dir {
      CustodyPathAsDeclared => []
      CustodyPathWrongOwner => [concat("dir ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathForbiddenBits => [concat("dir ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathModeNotDeclared => [concat("dir ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathAbsent => [concat("dir ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row)))]
      CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: _ } => [concat("dir ", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row)))]
    }),
    match readback.upper_ancestors {
      PathsRootOnly => []
      PathsNotRootOnly { paths: _, detail: _ } => [concat("ancestors ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.upper_ancestors))]
      PathsUnobservable { reason: _ } => [concat("ancestors ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.upper_ancestors))]
      PathsNotApplicable => [concat("ancestors ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: readback.upper_ancestors))]
    }),
    match readback.content {
      HostFileIdentical => []
      HostFileDiffers => [concat("content ", content_standing_wire(s: readback.content))]
      HostFileAbsent => [concat("content ", content_standing_wire(s: readback.content))]
      HostFileUnobservable { reason: _ } => [concat("content ", content_standing_wire(s: readback.content))]
    }),
    match readback.staging {
      StagingAbsent => []
      StagingResiduePresent { path: _ } => [concat("staging ", staging_residue_wire(s: readback.staging))]
      StagingUnobservable { reason: _ } => [concat("staging ", staging_residue_wire(s: readback.staging))]
    }),
    match readback.readers {
      CustodyReadersNotDeclared => []
      CustodyReadersAsDeclared { group: _ } => []
      CustodyReadersUnexpectedMember { group: _, unexpected: _ } => [concat("readers ", custody_readers_wire(s: readback.readers))]
      CustodyReadersMissingMember { group: _, missing: _ } => [concat("readers ", custody_readers_wire(s: readback.readers))]
      CustodyReadersGroupAbsent { group: _ } => [concat("readers ", custody_readers_wire(s: readback.readers))]
      CustodyReadersUnobservable { group: _, reason: _ } => [concat("readers ", custody_readers_wire(s: readback.readers))]
    })
  if length(causes) == 0 { CustodyHeld } else { CustodyNotHeld { causes: causes } }
}

// ── The decision before any write (pure) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

type CustodyAction
  = CustodyLeaveInPlace
  | CustodyWrite
  | CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: Secret }
  | CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace
  | CustodyCreateOnly
  | CustodyActionRefused { reason: String }

// THE HOST-AUTHORITATIVE DECISION, layered on the store-authoritative one rather than beside it: the
// directory, ancestor and metadata decisions are the same, and only a file that is already there and
// DIFFERS from the store is decided differently. It is never overwritten. If its refresh token moved
// on, it is owed to the store; if not, the host copy is merely fresher in its short-lived tokens and
// is left alone; if it now names another account or cannot be read, the converge refuses.
fn host_authoritative_differing_action(decision: CodexHarnessWriteBackDecision?) -> CustodyAction {
  match decision {
    Absent => CustodyActionRefused { reason: "host-authoritative file differs from the store and was not read back" }
    Present { value: d } =>
      match d {
        CodexHarnessWriteBackNotOwed => CustodyLeaveInPlace
        CodexHarnessWriteBackOwed { payload } => CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: payload }
        CodexHarnessWriteBackRefused { cause } =>
          CustodyActionRefused { reason: concat("host file not written back: ", codex_harness_write_back_refusal_wire(cause: cause)) }
      }
  }
}

fn host_authoritative_custody_action(base: CustodyAction, content: RunnerHostFileStanding, decision: CodexHarnessWriteBackDecision?) -> CustodyAction {
  match base {
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: _ } => base
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: _ } => base
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => base
    CustodyCreateOnly => base
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => host_authoritative_settled_action(base: base, content: content, decision: decision)
    CustodyWrite => host_authoritative_settled_action(base: base, content: content, decision: decision)
  }
}

fn host_authoritative_settled_action(base: CustodyAction, content: RunnerHostFileStanding, decision: CodexHarnessWriteBackDecision?) -> CustodyAction {
  match content {
    HostFileDiffers => host_authoritative_differing_action(decision: decision)
    HostFileIdentical => host_authoritative_metadata_action(base: base)
    HostFileAbsent => host_authoritative_first_placement_action(base: base)
    HostFileUnobservable { reason: _ } => base
  }
}

// A HOST-AUTHORITATIVE FILE IS NEVER REPLACED FROM THE STORE, whatever the reason the ordinary
// decision gave. Identical content with wrong owner or mode is repaired in place (chown and chmod on
// the path, no content written): the store-to-host content write stages the STORE bytes and renames
// them over the live file, so a refresh that moved the host file on between observation and rename
// would be lost -- the rename is outside the codex turn lock.
fn host_authoritative_metadata_action(base: CustodyAction) -> CustodyAction {
  match base {
    CustodyWrite => CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => base
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => base
    CustodyCreateOnly => base
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: _ } => base
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: _ } => base
  }
}

// FIRST PLACEMENT PUBLISHES CREATE-ONLY: a file that appears after the absence was observed (codex
// logged in by hand, or a racing converge) makes the publication fail and is left as found.
fn host_authoritative_first_placement_action(base: CustodyAction) -> CustodyAction {
  match base {
    CustodyWrite => CustodyCreateOnly
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => base
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => base
    CustodyCreateOnly => base
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: _ } => base
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: _ } => base
  }
}

fn custody_action(
  dir: CustodyPathMetadata,
  upper_ancestors: RunnerHostPathMetadata,
  content: RunnerHostFileStanding,
  file: CustodyPathMetadata,
) -> CustodyAction {
  match upper_ancestors {
    PathsRootOnly =>
      match dir {
        CustodyPathAsDeclared =>
          match content {
            HostFileUnobservable { reason: r } => CustodyActionRefused { reason: concat("content unobservable: ", r) }
            HostFileAbsent => CustodyWrite
            HostFileDiffers => CustodyWrite
            HostFileIdentical =>
              match file {
                CustodyPathAsDeclared => CustodyLeaveInPlace
                CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r } => CustodyActionRefused { reason: concat("file metadata unobservable: ", r) }
                CustodyPathWrongOwner => CustodyWrite
                CustodyPathForbiddenBits => CustodyWrite
                CustodyPathModeNotDeclared => CustodyWrite
                CustodyPathAbsent => CustodyWrite
              }
          }
        CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r } => CustodyActionRefused { reason: concat("directory metadata unobservable: ", r) }
        CustodyPathWrongOwner => CustodyActionRefused { reason: "directory is not as the row declares it" }
        CustodyPathForbiddenBits => CustodyActionRefused { reason: "directory is not as the row declares it" }
        CustodyPathModeNotDeclared => CustodyActionRefused { reason: "directory is not as the row declares it" }
        CustodyPathAbsent => CustodyActionRefused { reason: "directory is not as the row declares it" }
      }
    PathsNotRootOnly { paths: _, detail: _ } => CustodyActionRefused { reason: concat("an ancestor directory is not root-only: ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: upper_ancestors)) }
    PathsUnobservable { reason: _ } => CustodyActionRefused { reason: concat("an ancestor directory is not root-only: ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: upper_ancestors)) }
    PathsNotApplicable => CustodyActionRefused { reason: concat("an ancestor directory is not root-only: ", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: upper_ancestors)) }
  }
}

fn custody_action_wire(a: CustodyAction) -> String {
  match a {
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => "left-in-place"
    CustodyWrite => "written"
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: _ } => "written-back-to-store"
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => "metadata-repaired-in-place"
    CustodyCreateOnly => "created-only"
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: r } => concat("REFUSED ", r)
  }
}

// ── Remote legs (argv pure, execution effectful) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

fn custody_find_argv(path: String, kind: String, clause: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  concat(["find", path, "-maxdepth", "0", "-type", kind], clause)
}

fn custody_dir_ensure_argv(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, dir: String) -> List<String> {
  ["install", "-d", "-o", row.dir_ownership.user as String, "-g", row.dir_ownership.group as String, "-m", custody_dir_exact_perm(m: row.dir_mode), dir]
}

// converge_typed_remote_file writes as root and carries no ownership, so the row's owner and group
// are applied after the rename. Between the two the file is root:root at the arm's mode -- narrower
// than declared, never wider.
fn custody_file_chown_argv(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow) -> List<String> {
  chown_argv(owner: ChownOwnerNames { names: row.file_ownership }, path: row.path as String)
}

fn custody_chown_argv_at(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, path: String) -> List<String> {
  chown_argv(owner: ChownOwnerNames { names: row.file_ownership }, path: path)
}

fn custody_chmod_argv_at(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, path: String) -> List<String> {
  [chmod_path_resolved_program as String, remote_file_mode_octal(mode: custody_file_remote_mode(m: row.file_mode)), path]
}

fn staging_remove_argv(staging: String) -> List<String> {
  ["rm", "-f", "--", staging]
}

fn elevated(argv: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  remote_file_privileged_argv(privilege: RemoteFileViaNonInteractiveSudo, argv: argv)
}

// THE SUBJECT OF A CUSTODY CONVERGE IS A HOST, NOT A SLOT POPULATION (gunbc#11902). A credential's
// location, its administrator target and its custody do not depend on how many runner slots a host
// admits, so the subject resolves from gunbc.runner_host_deploy runner_host_spec_for rather than from
// an admitted RunnerHostDeploy, which refuses a host whose width is unresolved. The privilege law is
// kept: the writer may not be the account CI jobs run as, asked of gunbc.runner_host_grants over the
// spec's job_user rather than re-spelled (DESIGN §3).
type CustodyHost {
  host: HostIdentity
  target: SshTarget
  job_user: NonEmptyStr
}

type CustodyHostSubject
  = CustodyHostSubjectAdmitted { subject: CustodyHost }
  | CustodyHostSubjectRefused { cause: String }

fn custody_host(host: HostIdentity) -> CustodyHostSubject {
  match runner_host_spec_for(host: host) {
    RunnerHostSpecAbsent { host: h } =>
      CustodyHostSubjectRefused {
        cause: join(["host_credential_custody_converge: ", h as String, " has no runner host spec, so it is not a runner host"], ""),
      }
    RunnerHostSpecFound { spec: spec } =>
      if !bootstrap_principal_is_not_the_job_user(bootstrap: executor_bootstrap_principal, job_user: spec.job_user) {
        CustodyHostSubjectRefused {
          cause: join([
            "host_credential_custody_converge: the administrator principal ", executor_bootstrap_principal.login as String,
            " is the job user on ", host as String,
            ", so the account that places a credential would be the one CI jobs run as",
          ], ""),
        }
      } else {
        CustodyHostSubjectAdmitted {
          subject: CustodyHost { host: host, target: administrator_ssh_target(host: host), job_user: spec.job_user },
        }
      }
  }
}

type ElevatedLeg
  = ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: Int, stdout: String, stderr: String }
  | ElevatedLegRefused { reason: String }

// Every leg is elevated: the directory admits root and at most the row's group, so an unprivileged
// find or test inside it would report the permission boundary as an answer.
fn run_elevated_leg(
  subject: CustodyHost,
  context: FleetSshExecutionContext,
  argv: List<String>,
  stdin_payload: String,
) -> ElevatedLeg
{
  match typed_remote_file_step(target: subject.target, context: context, raws: elevated(argv: argv), stdin_payload: stdin_payload) {
    TypedRemoteFileStepArgvRefused => ElevatedLegRefused { reason: "argv refused as non-portable under the far-side shell re-parse allowlist" }
    TypedRemoteFileStepLegRefused { cause: why } => ElevatedLegRefused { reason: why as String }
    TypedRemoteFileStepRan { result: r } => ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: r.exit_code, stdout: r.stdout, stderr: r.stderr }
  }
}

type FindAnswer
  = FindPrinted
  | FindSilent
  | FindUnobservable { reason: String }

fn classify_find_answer(path: String, exit_code: Int, stdout: String, stderr: String) -> FindAnswer {
  if exit_code != 0 {
    FindUnobservable { reason: join(["find exit=", to_string(exit_code), " ", trim(s: stderr)], "") }
  } else if any(split(s: stdout, delimiter: "\n"), l => trim(s: l) == path) {
    FindPrinted
  } else {
    FindSilent
  }
}

fn find_answer(
  subject: CustodyHost,
  context: FleetSshExecutionContext,
  path: String,
  kind: String,
  clause: List<String>,
) -> FindAnswer
{
  match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: custody_find_argv(path: path, kind: kind, clause: clause), stdin_payload: "") {
    ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => FindUnobservable { reason: r }
    ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e } => classify_find_answer(path: path, exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e)
  }
}

fn find_printed(a: FindAnswer) -> Bool {
  match a {
    FindPrinted => true
    FindSilent => false
    FindUnobservable { reason: _ } => false
  }
}

fn find_unobservable_reason(a: FindAnswer) -> String? {
  match a {
    FindUnobservable { reason: r } => Present { value: r }
    FindPrinted => none
    FindSilent => none
  }
}

fn observe_custody_path(
  subject: CustodyHost,
  context: FleetSshExecutionContext,
  path: String,
  legs: CustodyPathLegs,
) -> CustodyPathMetadata
{
  match find_answer(subject: subject, context: context, path: path, kind: legs.kind, clause: []) {
    FindUnobservable { reason: r } =>
      match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: ["test", "-e", path], stdin_payload: "") {
        ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: _, stderr: _ } =>
          if c == 1 { CustodyPathAbsent } else { CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r } }
        ElevatedLegRefused { reason: _ } => CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r }
      }
    FindSilent => CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: concat(concat("exists but is not of type ", legs.kind), ", or find printed nothing") }
    FindPrinted => {
      let owned = find_answer(subject: subject, context: context, path: path, kind: legs.kind, clause: custody_owner_clause(o: legs.ownership))
      let open = find_answer(subject: subject, context: context, path: path, kind: legs.kind, clause: custody_perm_clause(perm: legs.forbidden_perm))
      let exact = find_answer(subject: subject, context: context, path: path, kind: legs.kind, clause: custody_perm_clause(perm: legs.exact_perm))
      match find_unobservable_reason(a: owned) {
        Present { value: r } => CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r }
        Absent => match find_unobservable_reason(a: open) {
          Present { value: r } => CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r }
          Absent => match find_unobservable_reason(a: exact) {
            Present { value: r } => CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r }
            Absent => classify_custody_path(reading: CustodyFindReading {
              owned_as_declared: find_printed(a: owned),
              forbidden_bits: find_printed(a: open),
              exact_mode: find_printed(a: exact),
            })
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn observe_upper_ancestors(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, paths: List<String>) -> RunnerHostPathMetadata
{
  match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: runner_host_root_only_find_argv(paths: paths, kind: "d"), stdin_payload: "") {
    ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => PathsUnobservable { reason: r }
    ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e } => classify_root_only_paths(requested: paths, exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e)
  }
}

// PRESENCE FROM THE PARENT LISTING, NOT `test -e`. gunbc#11845 deleted classify_host_file_presence
// because `test -e` exit 1 collapses ENOENT with EACCES, ELOOP and EIO; absence is now read from an
// elevated listing of the parent that SUCCEEDED (member_observe's argv and membership read), and a
// listing that did not succeed is unobservable, never absent. A present file is then compared by the
// same far-side `cmp -s -` judgment converge_typed_remote_file mints from, so observation and apply
// agree on "identical".
fn observe_custody_content(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, write: TypedRemoteFileWrite) -> RunnerHostFileStanding
{
  let path = write.path as String
  match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: parent_listing_argv(parent: path_parent(path: path)), stdin_payload: "") {
    ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => HostFileUnobservable { reason: concat("parent not listed: ", r) }
    ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: lc, stdout: lo, stderr: le } =>
      if lc != 0 {
        HostFileUnobservable { reason: join(["parent listing exit=", to_string(lc), " ", trim(s: le)], "") }
      } else if !listing_contains_entry(stdout: lo, name: path_basename(path: path)) {
        HostFileAbsent
      } else {
        match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: typed_remote_file_compare_argv(write: write), stdin_payload: write.content) {
          ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => HostFileUnobservable { reason: r }
          ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: cc, stdout: _, stderr: ce } =>
            runner_host_file_standing_of_report(
              report: classify_typed_remote_file_comparison(write: write, compare_exit_code: cc, compare_stderr: ce),
            )
        }
      }
  }
}

// REMOVE, THEN READ THE ABSENCE BACK FROM THE PARENT LISTING. Every value the legs use derives from
// the seal, including the residue predicate's key, so a mismatched name cannot read a listing that
// CONTAINS the residue as absence.
fn clear_staging(
  authorization: StagingCleanupAuthorization,
  context: FleetSshExecutionContext,
) -> StagingResidue
{
  let subject = authorization.subject
  let staging = authorization.staging
  let staging_parent = authorization.parent
  let staging_name = path_basename(path: staging)
  match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: staging_remove_argv(staging: staging), stdin_payload: "") {
    ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => StagingUnobservable { reason: concat("staging removal not run: ", r) }
    ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: rc, stdout: _, stderr: re } =>
      if rc != 0 {
        StagingUnobservable { reason: join(["staging removal exit=", to_string(rc), " ", trim(s: re)], "") }
      } else {
        match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: parent_listing_argv(parent: staging_parent), stdin_payload: "") {
          ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => StagingUnobservable { reason: concat("staging parent not listed: ", r) }
          ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e } =>
            if c != 0 {
              StagingUnobservable { reason: join(["staging parent listing exit=", to_string(c), " ", trim(s: e)], "") }
            } else {
              classify_staging_residue(path: staging, name: staging_name, stdout: o)
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

// ── The converge for one host ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

type CustodyRun {
  host: HostIdentity
  row: HostCredentialCustodyRow
  sm_version: SmResolvedVersionIdentity
  action: CustodyAction
  write_refusal: String?
  store_write_back: CodexHarnessWriteBackReceipt?
  readback: CustodyReadback
}

fn apply_custody_dir(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, dir: String) -> CustodyPathMetadata
{
  match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: custody_dir_ensure_argv(row: row, dir: dir), stdin_payload: "") {
    ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: concat("directory ensure not run: ", r) }
    ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: _, stderr: e } =>
      if c != 0 {
        CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: join(["directory ensure exit=", to_string(c), " ", trim(s: e)], "") }
      } else {
        observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row))
      }
  }
}

fn ensure_custody_dir(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, dir: String) -> CustodyPathMetadata
{
  match observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row)) {
    CustodyPathAsDeclared => CustodyPathAsDeclared
    CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r } => CustodyPathUnobservable { reason: r }
    CustodyPathWrongOwner => apply_custody_dir(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, dir: dir)
    CustodyPathForbiddenBits => apply_custody_dir(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, dir: dir)
    CustodyPathModeNotDeclared => apply_custody_dir(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, dir: dir)
    CustodyPathAbsent => apply_custody_dir(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, dir: dir)
  }
}

fn write_and_own(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, write: TypedRemoteFileWrite) -> String?
{
  match converge_typed_remote_file(
    target: subject.target,
    context: context,
    admission: TypedRemoteFileWriteAdmitted { write: write },
    mode: custody_file_remote_mode(m: row.file_mode),
    privilege: RemoteFileViaNonInteractiveSudo,
  ) {
    TypedRemoteFileConvergenceRefused { step: st, reason: why } => Present { value: join(["step=", st, " ", why], "") }
    TypedRemoteFileConverged { converged: _ } =>
      match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: custody_file_chown_argv(row: row), stdin_payload: "") {
        ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => Present { value: concat("step=owner not run: ", r) }
        ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: _, stderr: e } =>
          if c != 0 { Present { value: join(["step=owner exit=", to_string(c), " ", trim(s: e)], "") } } else { none }
      }
  }
}

type CustodyLeg {
  argv: List<String>
  stdin_payload: String
}

fn run_legs_until_refused(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, legs: List<CustodyLeg>, step: String) -> String? {
  fold(legs, init: none, f: (acc, leg) =>
    match acc {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent =>
        match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: leg.argv, stdin_payload: leg.stdin_payload) {
          ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => Present { value: join(["step=", step, " not run: ", r], "") }
          ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: _, stderr: e } =>
            if c != 0 { Present { value: join(["step=", step, " exit=", to_string(c), " ", trim(s: e)], "") } } else { none }
        }
    }
  )
}

fn observe_custody_readers(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, declared: CustodyReaderSet?) -> CustodyReadersStanding {
  match declared {
    Absent => CustodyReadersNotDeclared
    Present { value: d } =>
      match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: custody_getent_group_argv(group: d.group), stdin_payload: "") {
        ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => CustodyReadersUnobservable { group: d.group, reason: r }
        ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e } => classify_custody_readers(declared: declared, exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e)
      }
  }
}

fn add_member_legs(group: NonEmptyStr, add: List<String>) -> List<CustodyLeg> {
  map(add, login => CustodyLeg { argv: custody_group_add_member_argv(group: group, login: login), stdin_payload: "" })
}

// The refusal string, when the readers could not be made ready; none when nothing was owed or it landed.
fn apply_custody_readers(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, action: CustodyReadersAction) -> String? {
  match action {
    CustodyReadersNothingToDo => none
    CustodyReadersRefused { reason: r } => Present { value: r }
    CustodyReadersAdd { group: g, add: a } =>
      run_legs_until_refused(subject: subject, context: context, step: "reader-members", legs: add_member_legs(group: g, add: a))
    CustodyReadersCreateAndAdd { group: g, add: a } =>
      run_legs_until_refused(
        subject: subject, context: context, step: "reader-group",
        legs: concat([CustodyLeg { argv: custody_groupadd_argv(group: g), stdin_payload: "" }], add_member_legs(group: g, add: a)),
      )
  }
}

// METADATA ONLY: owner then mode on the existing path; the content is never touched.
fn repair_metadata_in_place(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, row: HostCredentialCustodyRow) -> String? {
  run_legs_until_refused(
    subject: subject, context: context, step: "metadata",
    legs: [
      CustodyLeg { argv: custody_chown_argv_at(row: row, path: row.path as String), stdin_payload: "" },
      CustodyLeg { argv: custody_chmod_argv_at(row: row, path: row.path as String), stdin_payload: "" },
    ],
  )
}

// CREATE-ONLY PUBLICATION: stage the store bytes beside the path, give the STAGED file the row's final
// owner and mode, then publish with a hard link, which fails when the destination exists rather
// than replacing it. A file that appeared after the absence observation therefore survives and the
// converge refuses; the staging sibling is removed afterwards by the shared staging cleanup.
fn create_only_publish(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, write: TypedRemoteFileWrite) -> String? {
  let staging = typed_remote_file_staging_path(write: write)
  run_legs_until_refused(
    subject: subject, context: context, step: "create-only",
    legs: [
      CustodyLeg { argv: typed_remote_file_stage_argv(write: write), stdin_payload: typed_remote_file_write_stdin_payload(write: write) },
      CustodyLeg { argv: custody_chown_argv_at(row: row, path: staging), stdin_payload: "" },
      CustodyLeg { argv: custody_chmod_argv_at(row: row, path: staging), stdin_payload: "" },
      CustodyLeg { argv: ["ln", "-T", staging, row.path as String], stdin_payload: "" },
    ],
  )
}

// THE ANCESTORS ARE OBSERVED BEFORE ANY MUTATION (gunbc#11902): ensure_custody_dir creates, so it
// runs only once the ancestors read root-only; otherwise the directory is only observed and the same
// pure custody_action decides.
// THE HOST FILE AS THE HOST HOLDS IT, read only for a host-authoritative row whose content already
// differs from the store. A failed read is an indeterminate observation, never an empty file.
fn read_host_custody_file(subject: CustodyHost, context: FleetSshExecutionContext, path: String) -> extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io.FilesystemFileObservation
{
  match run_elevated_leg(subject: subject, context: context, argv: ["cat", path], stdin_payload: "") {
    ElevatedLegRefused { reason: r } => FilesystemFileIndeterminate { cause: concat("host file read not run: ", r) }
    ElevatedLegRan { exit_code: c, stdout: o, stderr: e } =>
      if c != 0 {
        FilesystemFileIndeterminate { cause: join(["host file read exit=", to_string(c), " ", trim(s: e)], "") }
      } else {
        FilesystemFileRead { path: path, content: o }
      }
  }
}

type HostAuthoritativeReading {
  decision: CodexHarnessWriteBackDecision?
  host_content: String?
}

fn read_host_authoritative(
  subject: CustodyHost,
  context: FleetSshExecutionContext,
  row: HostCredentialCustodyRow,
  store_payload: Secret,
  content: RunnerHostFileStanding,
) -> HostAuthoritativeReading
{
  match content {
    HostFileDiffers =>
      match codex_harness_auth_read(content: store_payload as String) {
        CodexHarnessAuthRefused { cause: _ } => HostAuthoritativeReading { decision: none, host_content: none }
        CodexHarnessAuthAdmitted { identity } => {
          let observed = read_host_custody_file(subject: subject, context: context, path: row.path as String)
          HostAuthoritativeReading {
            decision: Present { value: codex_harness_write_back_decision(materialized: identity, read_back: observed) },
            host_content: host_custody_file_content(observed: observed),
          }
        }
      }
    HostFileIdentical => HostAuthoritativeReading { decision: none, host_content: none }
    HostFileAbsent => HostAuthoritativeReading { decision: none, host_content: none }
    HostFileUnobservable { reason: _ } => HostAuthoritativeReading { decision: none, host_content: none }
  }
}

fn host_custody_file_content(observed: extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io.FilesystemFileObservation) -> String? {
  match observed {
    FilesystemFileRead { path: _, content: c } => Present { value: c }
    FilesystemFileAbsent(_) => none
    FilesystemFileIndeterminate { cause: _ } => none
    FilesystemFileObservationsDisagree { path: _, cause: _ } => none
    FilesystemFileSubjectRefused { directory: _, name: _, cause: _ } => none
  }
}

// The content readback against the bytes the action left authoritative: the store's for a write or a
// leave-in-place on identical content; the host file's own bytes, read again, for a host-authoritative
// copy that was left or written back. The second is a re-read of the host, not an assumption about it.
fn observe_custody_content_against(
  subject: CustodyHost,
  context: FleetSshExecutionContext,
  row: HostCredentialCustodyRow,
  key_dir: NonEmptyStr,
  store_write: TypedRemoteFileWrite,
  authoritative_content: String?,
) -> RunnerHostFileStanding
{
  match authoritative_content {
    Absent => observe_custody_content(subject: subject, context: context, write: store_write)
    Present { value: c } =>
      match typed_remote_file_write_seal(path: row.path as FilePath, content: c, allowed_scope: FileTreeScope { root_path: key_dir }) {
        TypedRemoteFileWriteAdmissionRefused { cause: why } => HostFileUnobservable { reason: concat("host-authoritative readback not sealed: ", why as String) }
        TypedRemoteFileWriteAdmitted { write: w } => observe_custody_content(subject: subject, context: context, write: w)
      }
  }
}

// The reader group must exist and hold its declared members BEFORE the directory or file is chowned
// to it, and a refusal (undeclared member, unobservable group) stops every mutation below.
fn converge_host_credential_custody(
  subject: CustodyHost,
  context: FleetSshExecutionContext,
  placement_row: HostCredentialCustodyRow,
  key_dir: NonEmptyStr,
  upper_ancestors: List<String>,
  write: TypedRemoteFileWrite,
  store_payload: Secret,
  sm_version: SmResolvedVersionIdentity,
) -> CustodyRun
{
  let row = placement_row
  let staging = typed_remote_file_staging_path(write: write)
  let declared_readers = custody_reader_set(c: row.credential, job_user: subject.job_user)
  let readers_before = observe_custody_readers(subject: subject, context: context, declared: declared_readers)
  let readers_refusal = apply_custody_readers(
    subject: subject, context: context,
    action: custody_readers_action(declared: declared_readers, before: readers_before),
  )
  let readers_ready = match readers_refusal {
    Present { value: _ } => false
    Absent => true
  }
  let ancestors_before = observe_upper_ancestors(subject: subject, context: context, paths: upper_ancestors)
  let dir_before = match ancestors_before {
    PathsRootOnly => if !readers_ready {
      observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: key_dir as String, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row))
    } else {
      ensure_custody_dir(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, dir: key_dir as String)
    }
    PathsNotRootOnly { paths: _, detail: _ } => observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: key_dir as String, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row))
    PathsUnobservable { reason: _ } => observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: key_dir as String, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row))
    PathsNotApplicable => observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: key_dir as String, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row))
  }
  let content_before = observe_custody_content(subject: subject, context: context, write: write)
  let file_before = observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: row.path as String, legs: custody_file_legs(row: row))
  let base_action = custody_action(dir: dir_before, upper_ancestors: ancestors_before, content: content_before, file: file_before)
  let host_reading = match host_custody_authority(c: row.credential) {
    CustodyStoreAuthoritative => HostAuthoritativeReading { decision: none, host_content: none }
    CustodyHostAuthoritativeAfterPlacement =>
      read_host_authoritative(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, store_payload: store_payload, content: content_before)
  }
  let credential_action = match host_custody_authority(c: row.credential) {
    CustodyStoreAuthoritative => base_action
    CustodyHostAuthoritativeAfterPlacement =>
      host_authoritative_custody_action(base: base_action, content: content_before, decision: host_reading.decision)
  }
  let action = match readers_refusal {
    Present { value: r } => CustodyActionRefused { reason: r }
    Absent => credential_action
  }
  let write_refusal = match action {
    CustodyWrite => write_and_own(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, write: write)
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => repair_metadata_in_place(subject: subject, context: context, row: row)
    CustodyCreateOnly => create_only_publish(subject: subject, context: context, row: row, write: write)
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => none
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: _ } => none
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: _ } => none
  }
  let store_write_back = match action {
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload } => Present { value: codex_harness_add_version(token_source: WorkloadIdentityToken, payload: payload) }
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => none
    CustodyWrite => none
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => none
    CustodyCreateOnly => none
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: _ } => none
  }
  let authoritative_content = match action {
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: _ } => host_reading.host_content
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => host_reading.host_content
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => host_reading.host_content
    CustodyCreateOnly => none
    CustodyWrite => none
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: _ } => none
  }
  let staging_after = match admit_staging_cleanup(
    subject: subject,
    upper_ancestors: ancestors_before,
    dir: dir_before,
    key_dir: key_dir as String,
    staging: staging,
  ) {
    StagingCleanupAuthorized { authorization: z } => clear_staging(authorization: z, context: context)
    StagingCleanupWithheld { reason: r } => StagingUnobservable { reason: join([staging_cleanup_withheld_reason, ": ", r], "") }
  }
  let file_after = observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: row.path as String, legs: custody_file_legs(row: row))
  let dir_after = observe_custody_path(subject: subject, context: context, path: key_dir as String, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: row))
  let upper_ancestors_after = observe_upper_ancestors(subject: subject, context: context, paths: upper_ancestors)
  let content_after = observe_custody_content_against(
    subject: subject, context: context, row: row, key_dir: key_dir,
    store_write: write, authoritative_content: authoritative_content,
  )
  let readback = CustodyReadback {
    file: file_after,
    dir: dir_after,
    upper_ancestors: upper_ancestors_after,
    content: content_after,
    staging: staging_after,
    readers: observe_custody_readers(subject: subject, context: context, declared: declared_readers),
  }
  CustodyRun {
    host: subject.host,
    row: row,
    sm_version: sm_version,
    action: action,
    write_refusal: write_refusal,
    store_write_back: store_write_back,
    readback: readback,
  }
}

fn custody_run_settled(run: CustodyRun) -> Bool {
  let refused_before = match run.action {
    CustodyActionRefused { reason: _ } => true
    CustodyLeaveInPlace => false
    CustodyWrite => false
    CustodyRepairMetadataInPlace => false
    CustodyCreateOnly => false
    CustodyWriteBackToStore { payload: _ } => false
  }
  let write_failed = match run.write_refusal {
    Present { value: _ } => true
    Absent => false
  }
  let store_write_failed = match run.store_write_back {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: r } =>
      match r {
        CodexHarnessVersionAdded { version_name: _ } => false
        CodexHarnessStoreUnchanged => true
        CodexHarnessVersionAddRefused { detail: _ } => true
        CodexHarnessVersionAddAmbiguous { detail: _ } => true
        CodexHarnessWriteBackWithheld { cause: _ } => true
      }
  }
  let held = match host_credential_custody(row: run.row, readback: run.readback) {
    CustodyHeld => true
    CustodyNotHeld { causes: _ } => false
  }
  !refused_before && !write_failed && !store_write_failed && held
}

// NEVER THE BYTES. Every field below is metadata or a judgment; the content is named only by the
// Secret Manager version it was compared against. The last line restates the caveat on every
// receipt, because a receipt is what gets cited.
fn custody_receipt(run: CustodyRun) -> String {
  join([
    "HostCredentialCustodyReceipt credential=", host_custody_credential_wire(c: run.row.credential),
    " host=", run.host as String,
    " path=", run.row.path as String,
    " sm_version=", run.sm_version as String,
    "\n  action=", custody_action_wire(a: run.action),
    match run.write_refusal {
      Present { value: w } => concat(" write=REFUSED ", w)
      Absent => ""
    },
    match run.store_write_back {
      Present { value: r } => concat(" store=", codex_harness_write_back_receipt_wire(r: r))
      Absent => ""
    },
    "\n  file=", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: run.readback.file, legs: custody_file_legs(row: run.row)),
    "\n  dir=", custody_path_metadata_wire(m: run.readback.dir, legs: custody_dir_legs(row: run.row)),
    "\n  ancestors=", runner_host_path_metadata_wire(m: run.readback.upper_ancestors),
    "\n  content=", content_standing_wire(s: run.readback.content),
    "\n  staging=", staging_residue_wire(s: run.readback.staging),
    "\n  readers=", custody_readers_wire(s: run.readback.readers),
    "\n  custody=", match host_credential_custody(row: run.row, readback: run.readback) {
      CustodyHeld => "HELD"
      CustodyNotHeld { causes: cs } => concat("NOT-HELD ", join(cs, "; "))
    },
    "\n  scope=permission-bits readback only; NOT an observation that a non-declared principal is refused open",
    "\n",
  ], "")
}

// ── CI entry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// The dispatch input the fleet-converge workflow binds to this variable is a CHOICE over
// host_custody_credential_options, so the word that arrives here is a roster wire name or the run
// was never admitted by GitHub; select_host_custody_credential still refuses anything else.
data host_credential_custody_env_name: String = "FLEET_CONVERGE_CUSTODY_CREDENTIAL"

data host_credential_custody_attempt_raw: String = "host-credential-custody-converge-ci"

data host_credential_custody_receipt_path: String = "target/host-credential-custody-converge-receipt.txt"

fn write_receipt_then_exit(body: String, ok: Bool) -> ProcessExit {
  let w = Filesystem.Write(path: host_credential_custody_receipt_path, content: body)
  if w.success == false {
    exit_failure(reason: join(["host_credential_custody_converge: receipt write failed: ", w.error, "\n", body], ""))
  } else if ok {
    ExitSuccess
  } else {
    exit_failure(reason: body)
  }
}

type CustodyHostAdmission
  = CustodyHostAdmitted
  | CustodyHostRefused { cause: String }

fn custody_host_admission(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, host: HostIdentity) -> CustodyHostAdmission {
  match row.host_scope {
    CustodyAnyRunnerHost => CustodyHostAdmitted
    CustodyOnlyOnHost { host: only } =>
      if (only as String) == (host as String) {
        CustodyHostAdmitted
      } else {
        CustodyHostRefused {
          cause: join(["host_credential_custody_converge: ", host_custody_credential_wire(c: row.credential), " is delivered only to ", only as String, ", not ", host as String], ""),
        }
      }
  }
}

fn custody_fetch_refusal(row: HostCredentialCustodyRow, detail: String) -> ProcessExit {
  write_receipt_then_exit(body: join(["host_credential_custody_converge: ", host_custody_credential_wire(c: row.credential), " ", secret_ref_version_resource(ref: row.secret), " ", detail, "\n"], ""), ok: false)
}

// ONE HOST AND ONE CREDENTIAL PER RUN, BOTH NAMED BY THE DISPATCH. The subject (the administrator
// target, refusing a host with no runner host spec or whose administrator is the job user) is
// custody_host above. Row admission -- the credential
// selection, the host scope and the placement, including the group-traversal refusal -- runs
// before any Secret Manager read. The receipt is written on the failing path too.
fn host_credential_custody_converge_ci_wet() -> ProcessExit
{
  let stamp = concat("probed_at=", probed_at_word(reading: clock_now_probed_at()) as String)
  match actions_variable_read(name: host_credential_custody_env_name) {
    ActionsVariableAbsent { variable: v, detail: d } =>
      write_receipt_then_exit(body: join(["host_credential_custody_converge: ", v, " ", d, "; one rostered credential per run, named by the dispatch\n"], ""), ok: false)
    ActionsVariablePresent { value: raw_credential } =>
      match select_host_custody_credential(supplied: raw_credential) {
        HostCustodyCredentialUnrostered { supplied: s } =>
          write_receipt_then_exit(body: join(["host_credential_custody_converge: '", s, "' is not a rostered custody credential (", join(host_custody_credential_options, ", "), ")\n"], ""), ok: false)
        HostCustodyCredentialSelected { credential: credential } => {
          let row = host_credential_custody_row(c: credential)
          match actions_variable_read(name: fleet_converge_expected_host_env_name) {
            ActionsVariableAbsent { variable: v, detail: d } =>
              write_receipt_then_exit(body: join(["host_credential_custody_converge: ", v, " ", d, "; one host per run, named by the dispatch\n"], ""), ok: false)
            ActionsVariablePresent { value: raw_host } =>
              match custody_host_admission(row: row, host: raw_host as HostIdentity) {
                CustodyHostRefused { cause: c } => write_receipt_then_exit(body: concat(c, "\n"), ok: false)
                CustodyHostAdmitted =>
                  match custody_host(host: raw_host as HostIdentity) {
                    CustodyHostSubjectRefused { cause: c } => write_receipt_then_exit(body: concat(c, "\n"), ok: false)
                    CustodyHostSubjectAdmitted { subject: subject } =>
                      match custody_row_placement(row: row) {
                        CustodyPlacementRefused { cause: c } => write_receipt_then_exit(body: concat(custody_placement_refusal_wire(r: c), "\n"), ok: false)
                        CustodyPlaced { row: placed, key_dir: kd, upper_ancestors: ua } =>
                          match fetch_secret_ref_credential(secret_ref: placed.secret, token_source: WorkloadIdentityToken) {
                            SecretCredentialAccessUpsertRequired { plan: _ } =>
                              custody_fetch_refusal(row: placed, detail: "needs an accessor grant (gunbc.auth.fleet_secret_accessor_roster), which a CI run cannot apply")
                            SecretCredentialFetchRefused { reason: r } =>
                              custody_fetch_refusal(row: placed, detail: concat("token refused: ", r as String))
                            SecretCredentialWireDecodeRefused { identity_cause: _, payload_cause: _ } =>
                              custody_fetch_refusal(row: placed, detail: "AccessVersion response did not decode")
                            SecretCredentialResolvedVersionMismatch { requested: rq, resolved: rs } =>
                              custody_fetch_refusal(row: placed, detail: join(["requested ", rq, " but Secret Manager answered about ", rs], ""))
                            SecretCredentialReady { credential: material, resolved_version: version } =>
                              match typed_remote_file_write_seal(
                                path: placed.path as FilePath,
                                content: material as String,
                                allowed_scope: FileTreeScope { root_path: kd },
                              ) {
                                TypedRemoteFileWriteAdmissionRefused { cause: c } => write_receipt_then_exit(body: concat(c as String, "\n"), ok: false)
                                TypedRemoteFileWriteAdmitted { write: w } =>
                                  match prepare_fleet_ssh_agent_context(attempt_raw: host_credential_custody_attempt_raw) {
                                    FleetSshContextRefused { cause: c } => write_receipt_then_exit(body: concat(c, "\n"), ok: false)
                                    FleetSshContextReady { context: context, receipt: context_receipt } => {
                                      let run = converge_host_credential_custody(
                                        subject: subject, context: context, placement_row: placed, key_dir: kd,
                                        upper_ancestors: ua, write: w, store_payload: material, sm_version: version,
                                      )
                                      write_receipt_then_exit(
                                        body: join([stamp, "\n", context_receipt, custody_receipt(run: run)], ""),
                                        ok: custody_run_settled(run: run),
                                      )
                                    }
                                  }
                              }
                          }
                      }
                  }
              }
          }
        }
      }
  }
}
